{"title":"Fill in Subject Pronouns in Sentences","puid":"c-nateng-2-gb/r9bq4o","path":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05a-vgp-word/block-10-personal-pronouns-1/level-01","type":"normal","keyboardLayout":"standardNATENG","voiceLang":"en","voice":"f3_2025","instruction":{"voice":"m2_2025","speaker":true,"autoplay":true},"image":{"width":200},"trainers":[{"trainer":"contentCard","soundMode":"a","atoms":{"sound":"ssml: Do you know what a pronoun is?<break time='1000ms'/> Pronouns can replace nouns in sentences.<break time='1000ms'/> Let’s look at an example:","lsg":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05a-vgp-word/block-10-personal-pronouns-1/lsg/contentPlayer01.lsg"}},{"trainer":"content","textAlign":"center","onSamePage":true,"lsg":{"width":200},"atoms":[{"lsg":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05a-vgp-word/block-10-personal-pronouns-1/lsg/content01.lsg"},{"example":{"a":"<b>Amy</b> likes football. <br><b>She</b> likes football. ","b":"→  <m-blue>she</m-blue> = pronoun","sound":"ssml: Amy likes football. <break time='1200ms'/>She likes football. <break time='1200ms'/>'she'  is a pronoun. It replaces the noun 'Amy' in the sentence.","autoplay":true}},{"button":"Continue"},{"lsg":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05a-vgp-word/block-10-personal-pronouns-1/lsg/content02.lsg"},{"example":{"a":"<b>The boys</b> eat soup. <br><b>They</b> eat soup.","b":"→ <m-blue>they</m-blue> = pronoun","sound":"ssml: The boys eat soup. <break time='1200ms'/>They eat soup. <break time='1200ms'/>'they' is a pronoun. It replaces the noun 'boys' in the sentence.","autoplay":true}}]},{"trainer":"gap","gapMode":"buttons","instruction":{"text":"Choose the <b>pronoun</b> to complete the sentence."},"textAlign":"center","shuffleButtons":true,"shuffleAtoms":true,"soundMode":"a","atoms":[{"a":"Jenny swims in the pool.","b":"((++She It)) swims in the pool.","finishSound":"She swims in the pool.","image":"adobe_180891768_crop-1551-0-3546-3546"},{"a":"The children dress up.","b":"((++They I)) dress up.","finishSound":"They dress up.","image":"bigstockphoto_129359999_crop-1157-0-1400-1400"},{"a":"Liam runs fast.","b":"((++He We)) runs fast.","finishSound":"He runs fast.","image":"adobe_59148835"},{"a":"My mother and I plant flowers.","b":"((++We He)) plant flowers.","finishSound":"We plant flowers.","image":"adobe_111958690_crop-1091-0-3436-3436"},{"a":"The rabbit is called Fluffy.","b":"((++It We)) is called Fluffy.","finishSound":"It is called Fluffy.","image":"adobe_112707234"},{"a":"Does Emma like fruit?","b":"Does ((++she they)) like fruit?","finishSound":"Does she like fruit?","image":"adobe_164632150_crop-251-0-3456-3456"}]}],"parentTopic":{"title":"Vocabulary, Grammar and Punctuation - Word","path":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05a-vgp-word/topic","puid":"c-nateng-2-gb/70zwjh"},"parentBlock":{"title":"Personal Pronouns (1)","path":"/../c-nateng-2-gb/topic-05a-vgp-word/block-10-personal-pronouns-1/block","puid":"c-nateng-2-gb/9jjk4n"},"mediaFiles":{"sounds":[{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Does Emma like fruit?","etag":"93a5-8253"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Does she like fruit?","etag":"dc39-7389"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/He runs fast.","etag":"24a2-7389"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/It is called Fluffy.","etag":"0ba6-8973"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Jenny swims in the pool.","etag":"078c-9981"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Liam runs fast.","etag":"86d4-9549"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/My mother and I plant flowers.","etag":"d7f7-13005"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/She swims in the pool.","etag":"5ab4-10701"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The children dress up.","etag":"aba1-8397"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The rabbit is called Fluffy.","etag":"5666-11277"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/They dress up.","etag":"30e5-6381"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/We plant flowers.","etag":"538c-9549"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/ssml: Amy likes football. <break time='1200ms'/>She likes football. <break time='1200ms'/>'she'  is a pronoun. It replaces the noun 'Amy' in the sentence.","etag":"7599-57789"},{"fileId